# Curator of Destinies: "This spell can't be countered." Bot2's Counterspell may still target it and resolves, but Curator
# is not countered (the ruling). Its entry ability then looks at the top FIVE cards (Lightning Bolt, Plains, Counterspell,
# Forest, Mountain), Bot1 makes the Bolt and the Plains the face-down pile, and Bot2, the opponent chosen as it resolves,
# takes the face-up pile for Bot1: the Counterspell, the Forest and the Mountain go to Bot1's hand (revealed to every
# player), the face-down Bolt and Plains to its graveyard. Bot1 held its Moxen and Black Lotus for {4}{U}{U}.

